[Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  jerry dulac  he covers the steelers for the  pittsburgh post gazette hosts the  steelers radio network as well and kind  enough to join us  before he heads to camp i saw where ben  showed up clean-shaven-ish  and uh he had a shirt on that said  different there jerry so  um are you forced to then report on  write about how great ben looks now  well i will tell you dan that um despite  what people  think the last three or four years he  has come to camp  in wonderful shape you know he's had a  he's hired a nutritionist he's hired  trainer  he looks especially good now especially  trim  people forget he's a big man he's a six  foot five 250 pound guy  but i have to admit as well as he has  looked every year coming to camp he  looks  especially well and fit uh yesterday  certainly in that picture  is he the fourth best quarterback in his  own division  yeah i think that's a bunch of baloney  uh you know that's based on  um you know that that's just based on on  future possibilities  um you know but i mean ben's a proven  winner and  uh three super bowl appearances two  titles a number of playoff victories  um his numbers speak for themselves and  even last year dan i think  you know when you think they got off to  that 11-0 start he's coming off  major major elbow surgery and at one  point aft  after 11 weeks he's being talked about  an mvp candidate  forget about comeback player of the year  then he had that little slump and he had  a big second half in the indie game over  300 yards and three touchdowns  that uh snapped him out of that slump  and then after that uh  you know that terrible start uh against  the browns you know the bad snap on the  first play from scrimmage  you know in the second half again 330  yards three touchdowns made every throw  possible  um you know ben has still been okay yeah  he's 38 he's not the same guy he was  when he was 28.  but uh this idea that he's the fourth  best quarterback in the division  uh just based on future possibilities of  the young guys in the division  um to me as as a little far-fetched why  do you think there was some trepidation  it felt like maybe on the steelers part  of  is ben do they want him back and at what  price do you get him  is that a correct uh impression of of  what happened here  yeah absolutely and i will tell you that  uh ben actually thought that they were  um trying to make him make to force him  to make the decision for them um  i i was surprised on one hand  uh but not because they did eventually  do what i thought they would do  uh but um you know they knew they had to  do something with that salary cap hit  but wanting feeling that they were in  position to move on  from him uh with all the changes they  were making  or thought they were going to have to  make and as it turns out some of those  they didn't  i'm certainly not surprised that he's  back i expected that all along  but i have to admit that and i was a  little surprised that there was  some hesitation i always thought it  would be ben would go  out on ben's terms and nobody else's and  for a while it looked like  it looked like it wasn't going to be on  his terms  what did you make of their offseason in  pittsburgh  well the funny thing is is they thought  a lot of the changes were going to be on  offense and not on defense they thought  you know maybe ben was going to be gone  uh they knew they were going to move on  from james connor they thought juju  smith  uh schuster would be gone they knew  marquise pouncey was going to retire  and of course that happened and they did  move on from james connor but  the funny thing is is a lot of their  changes dan ended up being on defense  they lost three starters  um they kind of anticipated that that  might happen with bud dupree  and maybe even mike hilton but now you  throw in the retirement yesterday  of vince williams you know a guy that  they had released after the season  decided to bring back just to kind of  plug that hole for one more year  and then he retires on him so i think  their offense uh yeah there's a lot of  changes um you know they weren't  counting on david de castro  moving on from him that was injury  related  um so the changes on the offensive line  they kind of somewhat knew that was  going to happen but they didn't plan on  decastro  so some of those changes they counted on  some they didn't i think they're better  offensively  i think they're a little a little less  ferocious on defense  let me get a quick hit on the other  teams in the division let's start with  the bengals  what do you expect well until they  show that they can move up to be a 500  ball club um you know i'll wait and see  it's kind of like the browns two years  ago the browns had to show me they could  do it again  and they did um but i mean i like joe  burrow um i think he's going to be a  fantastic quarterback i hated to see the  injury last year you hate to see that  happen to any kind of promising young  star i think they'll be better  but i mean i think the browns are legit  and the ravens are the ravens the ravens  are very much like the steelers even  when you don't think they're going to be  very good  they're good that's just that's a salute  to their organization  um but there's no reason to think look  i'm not going to sit here and pronounce  the steelers are going to the super bowl  but as i tell everybody dan i mean who  would have thought they'd start 11-0  last year  who thought they'd go 12-4 and win a  division i could tell you  not too many people certainly around  here um and  my feeling has always been as long as  you have number seven you're not out of  any game and you're not out of any  season  jerry great to talk to you and hopefully  we'll catch up with you during the  season we appreciate your time  yeah dan anytime good to chat with you  all right jerry dulac he covers the  steelers  pittsburgh post gazette hosts the host  on the steelers radio network

